.TH 0C-UPDATE 1 "2026-10-27" "0c-ime 0.2.6" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
0c-update \- manage settings, vocabulary and models of the 0c Zhuyin input method
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B 0c-update
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B 0c-update
is the command-line front end of the 0c (\[u9748]\[u7280]\[u6CE8]\[u97F3])
Zhuyin input method.  It reads and changes the user's settings and personal
vocabulary, manages the optional neural models and starts the input engine.
.PP
On a system installation that is managed by the package manager, installing,
updating and removing 0c is done with
.BR apt (8);
the self-update commands of the upstream packages
.RB ( check ,
.BR install ,
.BR rollback ,
.BR uninstall ,
.BR schedule
and similar) are refused.
.PP
Most commands accept
.B \-json
to print a machine-readable result.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show the installed version, the state of the engine and a summary of the
current settings.
.TP
.B settings
List all settings with their current values and allowed values.
.TP
.BI set " key value " "[" key " " value " ...] [\-apply] [\-notify]"
Change settings.  With
.BR \-apply ,
a running engine is handed over to a new one so that the change takes
effect immediately.  Run
.B 0c-update settings
for the list of keys.  Keys fixed by a built-in input style must be changed
on a custom copy of that style (see
.BR profile ).
.TP
.BI profile " select|copy|rename|delete id " "[\-\-name " name "] [\-apply]"
Choose an input style.  Built-in styles (for example
.BR 0c ,
.BR microsoft ,
.BR macos )
are fixed;
.B copy
creates an editable custom style.
.TP
.BI vocab " command " [ arguments ]
Manage the personal vocabulary: add, list, remove and undo custom words and
phrases, and keep or forget learned phrases.  Run
.B 0c-update vocab
without arguments for the full list of commands.
.TP
.B models status|download|cancel|remove
Manage the optional neural selection and punctuation models in the user's
data directory.
.B download
fetches the pinned models from Hugging Face (about 260\ MB), verifies every
file and pairs them with the installed dictionary.  The models need
.BR python3 ,
.B python3-numpy
and
.BR python3-onnxruntime .
Without models the statistical engine is used.
.TP
.BI api " status|enable " "[\-port " port "]" " |disable|token \-regen|test"
Control the local HTTP API used by AI assistants; see
.BR 0c-mcp (1).
.TP
.B engine
Start the input engine if it is not running.
.TP
.BI open-settings " " [ page ]
Open the settings application.  The Debian packages do not ship it yet, so
this command reports that it is missing.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/0c/settings.json
User settings.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/zuin/
Personal vocabulary, learned phrases, downloaded models and API token.
.TP
.I /usr/share/0c/data/
System dictionary.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR 0c-mcp (1)
.PP
https://github.com/0c-biggo/0c-ime
